  "limits": [
    "Original 76 C-entry obligations remain separate from 31 core hooks. Row 75 receives direct bounded dialog-action semantics; rows 1/74 supporting coverage; zero whole rows closed, migration 141/661 unchanged.",
    "Help uses the existing generic dock identifier. No feature-specific manual page or external F1 help-content acceptance is claimed.",
    "Layer Presets has no GimpContext resource property. Only its GimpDocked get_preview slot is disabled; inherited context/menu/button/aux methods remain. Normal preview tab requests fall back to the registered layer icon.",
    "Actual-C UI controls create a real display and native factory/action wrapper, verify native image/display binding before manual context changes, three preview style constructions and icon normalization, source pixels/metadata/selected layer/count/clean state/Undo-Redo depth, no implicit Apply on open/re-raise/reopen/context reattachment, menu/cache weak destruction and Close Tab lifecycle.",
    "Programmatic selection and explicit menu Apply each produce one new layer with one Undo. These controls do not prove native pointer single-click event semantics, clone identity/source link, wrapper Refresh, or Undo/Redo top-object identity.",
    "Ordinary application one row click (one XTest press/release pair) created two clones and required two Undo steps; this remains an explicit next defect. Explicit Apply button created one clone, restored with one Undo. Opening/reopening alone preserved the two-layer image. No blanket usable-workflow or single-click correctness claim.",
    "Baseline ordinary quit exited SIGSEGV (-11). Source reveals a stranded child after failed wrapper construction, a plausible but unproven cause; no causal crash-fix claim. Candidate complete normal quit exited 0 without warnings/criticals.",
    "First capture excluded after wrong geometry field focused main window and typed shortcuts. Published visual baseline is second capture; all underlying failures remain retained.",
    "Full native v2 aggregate failed a mapped-widget assertion after display reuse although isolated action passed. Final fixture waits up to 2 seconds for natural mapping using weak observation, never shows widgets or alters config, retains mapped assertions; full aggregate rerun required.",
    "Native and ASan+UBSan run 36 source-registered cases each in 3 successful processes under unchanged 90/120 second bounds, no timeout multiplier. LeakSanitizer disabled. Two C consumers compile with cc under recorded project-default standard, no C++ override or explicit-C11 claim.",
    "No full GIMP suite, interactive multiwindow/F1/manual content, broader legacy ABI closure or blocked perspective guard integration. Overwrite/colorpicker/wrong-point/perspective gaps remain open."
  ],
